00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.679
What the hell with Twitter.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:12.850
What does that make NBC?

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.250
I don't know.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:19.000
Here is Tucker Carlson's announcement now
viewed nearly 20 million times.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.529
He made the announcement on Twitter, I guess,
partnering with Elon Musk to relaunch, telling

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:28.230
a number of corrosive lies.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.310
Let's take a look at Tucker's big announcement.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:36.629
Filmed in Ultra widescreen, they've never
seen widescreen this wide.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:39.460
Apparently from his cabin in Maine or Florida.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.460
Who knows?

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.460
Let's take a listen.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.150
Speaker 2: Hey, it's Tucker Carlson.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.860
You often hear people say the news is full
of lies.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.100
But most of the time, that's not exactly right.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.190
Much of what you see on television or read
The New York Times is, in fact, true.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.640
In the literal sense, it could pass one of
the media's own fact checks.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.950
Lawyers would be willing to sign off on it.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.200
In fact, they may have, but that doesn't make
it true.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.480
It's not true.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.141
At the most basic level, the news you consume
is a lie, a lie of the stealthy, highest and

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:10.380
most insidious kind.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.070
Facts have been withheld on purpose, along
with proportion and perspective.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.070
You are being manipulated.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.680
How does that work?

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.680
Let's see.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.310
If I tell you that a man has been unjustly
arrested for armed robbery, that is not, strictly

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.750
speaking, a lie.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.750
He may have been framed.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:29.080
At this point, there's been no trial, so no
one can really say.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.740
But if I don't mention the fact that the same
man has been arrested for the same crime six

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.740
times before.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.939
Am I really informing you?

00:01:36.939 --> 00:01:38.280
No, I'm not.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.810
I misleading you.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.159
And that's what the news media are doing.

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:48.590
Speaker 1: And what's really funny about this
is that it's a very fair criticism.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:53.619
Of the way that Fox News, including Tucker
Carlson, present news stories and have done

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:58.170
so since they launched and what it was in
1996 or 1997.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.320
It's quite I mean, he's right about everything
he's saying.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.190
The problem is he's as guilty as anyone of
exactly what he's calling out here.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:11.140
Speaker 2: Every story that matters every
day of the week, every week of the year.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.510
What's it like to work in a system like that
after more than 30 years in the middle of

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.510
it?

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.510
We could tell you stories.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.510
Speaker 1: What a victim.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:19.510
What a poor guy.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.220
Speaker 2: The best you can hope for in the
news business at this point is the freedom

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.970
to tell the fullest truth that you can.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.370
But there are always limits.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.450
And you know that if you bump up against those
limits often enough, you will be fired for

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.450
it.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:38.330
Speaker 1: So now Tucker is arguing he was
fired for bumping up against the limits valiantly

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.770
and bravely, trying to tell us the truth.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:45.400
But I guess someone didn't really want him
to do that or something.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:52.440
I mean, this you could only believe this if
you followed absolutely nothing of what's

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.700
been going on with Tucker Carlson for the
last decade.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.379
Speaker 2: That's not a guess.

00:02:56.379 --> 00:02:58.100
It's guaranteed.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:03.200
Every person who works in English language
media understands that the rule of what you

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.349
can't say defines everything.

00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:07.180
It's filthy, really.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.180
Right.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.730
And it's utterly corrupting.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:14.650
You can't have a free society if people aren't
allowed to say what they think is true.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.980
Speech is the fundamental prerequisite for
democracy.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.530
That's why it's enshrined in the first of
our constitutional amendments.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.560
Amazingly, as of tonight, there aren't many
platforms left that allow free speech.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.390
Speaker 1: There aren't.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.690
That's surprising to many people.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:32.390
Speaker 2: That's the big one remaining in
the world.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.140
The only one is Twitter.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.140
Speaker 1: How can where.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.340
Speaker 2: We are now?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.659
Twitter has long served as the place where
our national conversation incubates and develops.

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:43.480
Twitter is not a partizan site.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.110
Everybody's allowed here and we think that's
a good thing.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.780
And yet for the Who's this week, by the way,
was part.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.730
The news that you see analyzed on Twitter
comes from media organizations that are themselves

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.470
thinly disguised propaganda outlets like Fox.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.810
You see it on cable news.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.980
You talk about it on Twitter.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:06.500
The result may feel like a debate, but actually
the gatekeepers are still in charge.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.909
We think that's a bad system.

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:12.299
We know exactly how it works and we're sick
of it.

00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:15.480
Starting soon, we'll be bringing a new version
of the show we've been doing for the last

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.980
six and a half years to Twitter.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.509
We bring some other things, too, which we'll
tell you about.

00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:22.750
But for now, we're just grateful to be here.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.650
Free speech is the main right that you have.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.170
Without it, you have no others.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:28.170
Soon.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.250
Speaker 1: There you go.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.500
So Tucker Carlson bravely announcing that
he will be coming to Twitter.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:39.419
Now, I will mention that Elon Musk in response
to this tweeted, I want to be clear, we have

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:43.650
not signed a deal of any kind whatsoever.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.220
Tucker is subject to the same rules and rewards
of all content creators.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.880
Rewards means subscriptions and ad revenue
share.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.729
Still working on software needed for Ladder,
which is a function of how many people subscribe

00:04:55.729 --> 00:04:57.970
and the ad views associated with the content.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:02.009
I hope that many others, particularly from
the left, also choose to be content creators

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:03.009
on this platform.

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:05.720
Listen, I'd love to learn more about that.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.720
We've never been there's never been ad revenue
available to us that we've been aware of on

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.720
Twitter, which is interesting.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.720
I'd like to learn more.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.010
So listen, this is Tucker's big return.

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:19.760
I don't know to what extent this is the most
profitable avenue for him.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:20.940
I just don't know.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.650
I need to learn a little more about it.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:33.830
But it is very clear that this is the continued
refrain from the right that pre Elon Musk

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.600
Twitter was not for free speech.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.170
It was not a so-called free speech platform.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:42.830
The speech of conservatives was unfairly limited.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:48.730
But now we can all rejoice and pray at the
altar of Elon Musk because he has saved Twitter,

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.759
